# Normalize every text file to LF line endings on checkout and commit, regardless of each
# contributor's local Git config. Without this, Windows' `core.autocrlf=true` checks files out
# as CRLF while the repo's blobs (and ESLint/Prettier, which enforce LF) expect LF -- that
# mismatch is purely cosmetic (doesn't change how any code runs) but floods `npm run lint` with
# thousands of "Delete CR" errors across files nobody touched, and can make clean diffs noisy.
# This doesn't rewrite any existing blob by itself -- they're already LF -- it only fixes how
# Git checks files out and stages them from here on.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Known binary types: never touch line endings. `text=auto`'s own detection already skips these,
# but spelling out the common ones here means it never has to guess.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.webp binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.pdf binary
